ifficult to play if the game shifts to singles or straights.\n\nReason: Beating the teammate\'s 10s with Aces allows you to transition to a "1 card left" status. This pressures the Landlord to break a top pair (like 22) or lose the game immediately if they pass. It is the best chance to secure a win or cripple the Landlord\'s hand.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣A", "♦A"]}'}
